.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt NOLOGIN 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm nologin
.Nd politely refuse a login
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /sbin/nologin
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is meant to be the login shell, in
.Xr passwd 5 ,
of an account that must not log in, such as one a daemon runs as.
It writes a message to its standard output, logs the attempt with
.Xr syslog 3
at
.Dq auth.crit ,
naming the user and the terminal, and exits with status 1.
Any arguments, such as the
.Fl c Ar command
another program may pass to a shell, are ignored.
.Pp
The message is the contents of
.Pa /etc/nologin.txt
if that file exists, and otherwise
.Dq This account is currently not available.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/nologin.txt
.It Pa /etc/nologin.txt
The message to show, if present.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
always exits with status 1.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr login 1 ,
.Xr passwd 5 ,
.Xr syslog.conf 5
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
command appeared in
.Bx 4.4 .
OxideBSD's shows
.Pa /etc/nologin.txt
as
.Ox Ns 's
does, and logs the attempt as
.Fx Ns 's
does.
